# PART 5 — DELIVERY STATUS AND ORDER PROGRESS

Use the existing delivery note statuses:

- PREPARED
- IN_TRANSIT
- DELIVERED
- CANCELLED

Implement the necessary status update actions and UI controls.

When a delivery note becomes DELIVERED:

- Update the corresponding `order_items.quantity_delivered` values consistently.
- Recompute delivery progress without incrementing quantities twice.
- Update the parent order status.

Order status should follow the actual physical delivery progress:

- CONFIRMED: nothing physically delivered yet.
- PARTIALLY_DELIVERED: at least one quantity has been delivered, but the complete accepted PO has not been delivered.
- COMPLETED: all accepted PO quantities have been delivered.
- CANCELLED: only when the order is properly cancelled.

A PREPARED or IN_TRANSIT delivery note must reserve quantities but must not count as physically delivered.

Prevent invalid status transitions.

A delivered delivery note must not be cancelled as if the physical delivery had never happened.

If a prepared or in-transit delivery note is cancelled, safely release its reserved quantities.

If the associated invoice has already received a payment, do not silently cancel it. Respect the existing payment allocation and invoice cancellation rules.

When an unpaid invoice is cancelled together with a non-delivered delivery note, make sure both document states remain consistent.

Keep all status changes auditable.

